  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/dashdogy/RTX40MFG-Unlock/zipball/v1.4.1-hotfix.1",
  "body": "**V1.4.1-hotfix.1 fixes Witcher 3 path-traced HairWorks compatibility with ReShade and RenoDX.** It also fixes cases of hair disappearing after loading a save or moving to another area, and keeps hair diagnostics available throughout longer sessions for better bug reports.\n\nFor The Witcher 3 DirectX 12, install RTXMFG as **`winmm.dll`** beside `witcher3.exe`. Enable HairWorks, path tracing and **Path Traced Hair** in the game. **Fully restart the game after changing Path Traced Hair or Frame Generation.** Hair support remains experimental and requires a matching game and shader profile.\n\nThe ZIP contains only **RTXMFG.dll**, combining the backend and menu. For an existing single-DLL installation, close the game and replace the installed mod DLL, preserving its chosen filename and your settings. Press **Backspace** to open the menu. See the [README](https://github.com/dashdogy/RTX40MFG-Unlock/blob/v1.4.1-hotfix.1/README.md) for installation and supported filenames. SHA-256 checksums for the ZIP and extracted DLL are attached.\n\n**RTX 30 support remains very early and experimental.** The newer RTX 30 development changes are excluded from this hotfix. Vulkan support remains experimental; Dynamic MFG is unavailable on Vulkan.\n\nThe release DLL passed all 54 local release regression cases (2,131 assertions), plus hair CPU checks and eight synthetic GPU configurations against both supported Witcher builds. The ReShade resource-device and pool-pressure cases passed in every GPU configuration. This establishes build and harness validation. In-game ReShade/RenoDX hair rendering, repeated save loads and area changes, and long-session logging still await validation with this exact DLL.\n",
